# Supabase connection for the webapp (browser).
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in, or set the same variables in
# the Vercel project settings.
#
# With both set, the storefront catalogue reads Supabase, and the back office's
# product management (list, create, edit, images, stock, recommendations) reads
# and writes the database and the `product-media` bucket, with admin sign-in
# through Supabase Auth.
#
# Only the PUBLISHABLE key belongs here: it is shipped to every browser and all
# access is enforced by Row Level Security in Postgres. Never put the
# service_role / secret key in a VITE_ variable — Vite inlines every VITE_
# variable into the public bundle.
#
# Leave both empty to run the prototype on its built-in mock catalogue.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
